sentences.l:
“Old man, not yet him have dogs eaten, nor birds,
but still that one lies beside Achilles’ ship,
just so, among the huts;

Truly around the tomb of his own dear companion
he drags him uncaringly, when heavenly dawn has appeared,
and does not disfigure him;

you yourself would marvel, coming near,
how dewy he lies, and the blood about him has been washed away,
nor is he stained anywhere;

“O child, truly it is a good thing to give fitting gifts
to the immortals, since never my son, if ever he was,
forgot in the halls the gods who hold Olympus;

But when they came to the hut of Peleus’-son,
high, which the Myrmidons made for their lord,
having cut beams of fir;

and the two only,
the hero Automedon and Alcimus, scion of Ares,
bustled about, standing by;

and the one who was alone to me, and guarded the city and the men themselves,
him you a while ago killed, as he defended his native land,
Hector;
